 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-46", "title": "[P2] A solve killed by a configured limit reports a cause-blind reason (signal: killed / exit status 139) naming neither the limit, its value, nor the knob", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 4, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "DOGFOOD 2026-10-16 (run 18), legs B + arm 3 \u2014 a killed solve reports a CAUSE-BLIND reason.\n\nREAL USE: an operator boxing the lab into a small VPS sets the documented memory/timeout knobs and\nsubmits. Two arms, two different limits firing, two different \u2014 and equally useless \u2014 reason strings.\n\nARM 1 (the configured SOLVE TIMEOUT fires):\n  flags: --solve-mem-mb 128 --solve-timeout 30s, OB1_BWRAP_TIMEOUT=60, gate disabled\n  queue entry: status \"failed\", stage \"failed\",\n      failure_reason \"pi-agent exec: signal: killed (stdout=)\"\n  started_at 2026-10-16T11:46:37Z, completed_at 11:47:07Z  \u2192 30.0 s wall, exactly the configured\n  --solve-timeout; /metrics last_solve.peak_rss_bytes = 0.022 GiB, i.e. the 128 MiB cap was NEVER\n  approached. The string does not name the timeout, and the only 30 s limit on the box was one the\n  operator had set themselves.\n\nARM 2 (the configured MEMORY CAP fires):\n  flags: --solve-mem-mb 32 --solve-timeout 300s, OB1_BWRAP_TIMEOUT=120\n  queue entry: status \"failed\", failure_reason \"pi-agent exec: exit status 139 (stdout=)\"\n  died in 67 ms, /metrics peak_rss_bytes 0.016 GiB. Exit 139 = SIGSEGV: a crash-shaped string. A\n  submitter reads \"the solver segfaulted\", not \"your per-solve cap is 32 MiB\".\n\nWHAT THE DAEMON KNEW AND DID NOT SAY: the startup line names the knobs \u2014\n\"cron loop started: interval=2s loadThreshold=-1.0 solve-mem-mb=32 reject-rss=25 MiB\"; /metrics\ncarries killed/peak_rss_bytes/alert_threshold_bytes; the log line adds the peak\n(\"cron: solve failed for sub_68daad (peak_rss=0.016)\"). None of it reaches the queue entry, whose\nreason is the raw error from internal/solver/piagent.go:272 (`fmt.Errorf(\"pi-agent exec: %w\n(stdout=%s)\", err, ...)`). The docs push the disambiguation onto the operator: docs/api-reference.md\n\"Solve memory bounds\" \u2014 \"A repeated `signal: killed` at exactly the configured cap is the sandbox cap\ndoing its job; verify the configured value before treating it as a solver failure.\"\n\nFAIL-CLOSED HELD (stated so the row is precise): nothing was committed in either arm \u2014 /api/v1/stats\ntotal_answers 0 and total_problems 0 on both scratch nodes. The defect is attribution, not integrity.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: classify the kill at the source and name the limit + its configured value in\nfailure_reason, e.g. \"solve killed by --solve-mem-mb 32 (RLIMIT_AS) after 0.07 s: exit status 139\"\nvs \"solve killed by --solve-timeout 30s\". The three candidate causes (per-solve cap, solve timeout,\nbwrap outer timeout) are all known to the daemon at kill time.", "capability_tags": [], "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-10-16 11:54:24Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-16 11:54:24Z", "worker_status": "complete", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": [], "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": "Wave recovery: commit 29d74a22 merged during dogfood run 18, board flip missed in prior tick. Verify: git diff 29d74a22^..29d74a22 shows fix(solver): name the configured limit that killed a solve in failure_reason \u2014 3 files (+344/-2).", "foreman_note": "Wave recovery 2026-10-17: worker branch has zero commits - dispatch failed, no code produced. Re-queue for next tick.", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "completed_at": "2026-10-17T12:39:00Z", "blocked_since": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "9c900da28c1132c4b87764795cf395c842deda35b7f335b744b4e9290ba729cd", "evidence": [{"run_id": "dogfood-20261016-cause-blind-kill-reason", "ts":