-{"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-47", "title": "[P3] A normal gate skip logs as \"cron: tick error: cron: system is not idle\" on every tick \u2014 the steady state of a busy box reads as a permanent error", "status": "superseded", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "DOGFOOD 2026-10-16 (run 18), leg A \u2014 a normal gate decision is logged as an error, every tick.\n\nEVIDENCE (scratch node :18799, --mem-fraction 0.001 -cron-interval 2s, gate tripped by design):\n  $ grep -iE 'cron' serve.log | tail -8\n  2026/10/16 06:45:57 cron: tick error: cron: system is not idle\n  2026/10/16 06:45:59 cron: tick error: cron: system is not idle\n  ... 10 identical lines in 20 s (one per tick).\n\nThe same line is what the LIVE unit emits whenever this host is busy (it runs -cron-interval 60s), so\na busy box produces a permanent stream of \"tick error\" lines \u2014 including on a deployment whose whole\npoint is to wait for idle cycles.\n\nWHY IT IS A DEFECT: ErrNoIdle is a DECISION (internal/cron/loop.go:497 returns it from checkIdle), but\nRun logs every non-canceled tick error with the same prefix (internal/cron/loop.go:378-380\n`l.cfg.Logger.Printf(\"cron: tick error: %v\", err)`). An operator (or the fleet's own log scanners)\nkeying on \"tick error\" gets a false alarm at cron cadence exactly when the gate is working correctly,\nand the same prefix covers real failures (reap errors, dequeue errors, solve failures) with no way to\ntell them apart in aggregate.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: log gate skips on their own path \u2014 e.g. `cron: deferred \u2014 host busy (memory): used\n0.368 / threshold 0.001` (the reason string and the HostSnapshot already exist at that point) \u2014 and\nkeep \"tick error\" for genuine errors. Acceptance: with the gate tripped, N ticks produce N deferral\nlines and zero \"tick error\" lines.", "capability_tags": [], "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-10-16 11:54:39Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-16 11:54:39Z", "worker_status": "pending", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": [], "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": null, "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "completed_at": null, "blocked_since": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "c89b8ef30f20999506d9ed49356769000d8c3c687576ce845f4f0b9fc7ef31a3", "evidence": [{"run_id": "dogfood-20261016-gate-skip-logged-as-tick-error", "ts": "2026-10-16 11:54:39Z"}]}, "notes": "Resolved by DF-OFF-BY-ONE-45 commit 895c0861 \u2014 IdleGateError now logs deferment line and stamps queue entry instead of failing the tick"}
